:: Diana-P1-FirstStory-B {"position":"225,16725","size":"100,100"}
<<loc_Lobby>>\

    <<pic $diana>>\
    <<art $diana>>\

    <<switch $c>>\
        <<case 1>>\
            <<nm $player "I mean, I think around here it's safer to know too much than to not know enough.">>\
            
            ''$diana.name smiles.''
            
            <<nm $diana "I was hoping you'd say that! Follow me, let's talk in my office.">>\
            
            <<loc_RecordsOffice>>\
            
            ''You follow $diana.name into her office. She closes the door and pours you both a cup of tea before she relaxes into her chair.''
            
            <<nm $diana "Hm, I don't know why I feel so compelled to talk to you about this, now that I think about it...">>\
            
            <<nm $player "O-oh? Heh, I uh... I guess..." "Oh shit...">>\
            
            ''She sips at her tea.''
            
            <<nm $diana "I suppose it's just therapeutic. In any case, I was curious as to whether or not you've worked out how The Company operates from a logistical standpoint. Specifically, in the branch office locations in relation to central headquarters.">>\
            
            ''You think for a moment.''
            
            <<nm $player "I've... I mean I've never really thought about it. Most major corporations operate this way, right? A central office delegates operations to smaller satellite offices around the country, or world, so their business can expand without having to move resources around. Isn't that kind of a standard practice?">>\
            
            ''$diana.name smiles over her tea cup.''
            
            <<nm $diana "Precisely. We operate no differently than any other trade organization. The only real differences are the security measures we have in place, as well as the nature of our products and practices. From a business perspective we're quite ordinary, which is intentional, of course.">>\
            
            ''She sips at her tea and stands up, walking around her desk and running a finger along your shoulders.''
            
            <<nm $diana "Another key difference, the one I wanted to talk to you about specifically, is how The Company perceives 'trust'. Trust between employees, trust between offices... Do you trust your coworkers, $player.name?">>\
            
            ''Her breath against your ear is making you slightly dizzy, hazy.''
            
            <<nm $player "I-I... I mean, I work with you and $penny.name and $sophie.name every day. I'd like to think there's some trust between us?">>\
            
            <<nm $diana "Hm, oh sweetie... Your new line of work is such that failure to meet and exceed expectations can, and will, result in a situation where a quick death is the best case scenario... and also a very unlikely one.">>\
            
            ''She squeezes your shoulder.''
            
            <<nm $diana "Not a single, desperate, broken individual on this organization's payroll would hesitate to throw you to the wolves if it meant saving themselves. Not your cute little lab partner, not our fearless leader, and certainly not me.">>\
            
            ''Her grip loosens, and she sighs heavily as she sits back down across from you.''
            
            <<nm $diana "But that doesn't mean we can't look out for each other when our necks aren't on the chopping block. The truth is I'm quite fond of you, $player.name, and I'd hate for your naivety to be the end of you. If...">>\
            
            ''She pauses, adjusting her glasses.''
            
            <<nm $diana "When the time comes, I just want to make sure you're capable of looking out for yourself. Anyway, that's all. Perhaps we'll continue our conversation another time. For now, we have actual work to attend to.">>\
            
            <<nm $player "Y-yeah, $diana.name, thanks for the talk.">>\
            
            ''You're shown out of $diana.name's office, pretending not to notice her hand casually resting on your ass...''
            
            <<love $diana 5>>
            
            <<btnLink "Continue" "Work" "passTime()">>
        <<case 2>>\
            <<nm $player "Um, yeah, y'know, maybe it's best I don't know too much. Seems sticking your nose where it doesn't belong is liable to get you into a bad situation around here.">>\
            
            ''$diana.name's expression is both surprised, and somewhat impressed.''
            
            <<nm $diana "You're not wrong, $player.name, you're not wrong at all. Pity though, I do so enjoy our talks. Perhaps another time, then.">>\
            
            ''$diana.name leaves you standing in the hallway, the sound of her clicking heels vanishing off as she heads back to her office.''
            
            <<SetFlag $diana "SkipStory">>\
            <<btnLink "Continue" "Work">>
    <</switch>>\


